{
  "summary": "Extracts Guix cross-compilation toolchain definitions from manifest_build.scm into a dedicated toolchains.scm module, making them reusable across manifests. Introduces a separate linux_static.scm manifest used during Linux builds in guix-build, and adds the cross-toolchain to manifest_gui.scm. Updates guix-build to configure GUIX_PACKAGE_PATH so Guix can locate the new local module and patch files.",
  "problem": "Linux toolchain definitions were embedded directly inside manifest_build.scm, preventing developers from configuring alternate toolchains or building separate static environments independently.",
  "evidence": [
    "PR description: 'This is a prerequisite for static release builds (#25573). A split toolchain also allows us to make other builds changes, like #36193 (building a more stripped down libstdc++, and shipping smaller binaries).'"
  ],
